 = 2 + 4(1) = 6.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0005","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"Find the sum of the first three terms of the geometric sequence with first term 1 and ratio 2.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"7","option_c":"3","option_d":"4","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The terms are 1, 2, and 4; their sum is 7.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0006","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many ordered arrangements of 2 objects can be selected from 4 distinct objects?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"12","option_b":"8","option_c":"6","option_d":"16","correct_option":"a","explanation":"This is 4P2 = 4(3) = 12.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0007","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many unordered pairs can be chosen from 5 distinct students?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"20","option_b":"11","option_c":"10","option_d":"7","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The count is 5C2 = 5(4)/2 = 10.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0008","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"probability","chapter_title":"Probability","statement":"A box has 6 equally likely numbered slips, of which 1 is marked. What is the probability of drawing a marked slip?","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"1/6","option_b":"7/6","option_c":"5/6","option_d":"1/7","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Probability = favorable/total = 1/6 = 1/6.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0009","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"binomial-theorem","chapter_title":"Binomial Theorem","statement":"What is the coefficient of x^2 in the expansion of (1 + x)^4?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"12","option_b":"4","option_c":"10","option_d":"6","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The coefficient is 4C2 = 4(3)/2 = 6.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0010","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"trigonometry","chapter_title":"Trigonometry","statement":"For an acute angle theta, the opposite side is 3 and hypotenuse is 5. Find sin(theta).","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"4/5","option_b":"3/5","option_c":"5/3","option_d":"3/4","correct_option":"b","explanation":"sin(theta) = opposite/hypotenuse = 3/5 = 3/5.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0011","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions-and-limits","chapter_title":"Functions and Limits","statement":"Evaluate limit as x approaches 2 of (x^2 - 4)/(x - 2).","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"5","option_c":"2","option_d":"4","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Factor the numerator as (x - 2)(x + 2). The limit is 2 + 2 = 4.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0012","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"differentiation","chapter_title":"Differentiation","statement":"If f(x) = x^2 + 1x, find f'(1).","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"5","option_b":"2","option_c":"3","opti