 9. Hence the radius is 3.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0017","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"parabola","chapter_title":"Parabola","statement":"The parabola y^2 = 4x has focus at which point?","chapter_num":15,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"(-1, 0)","option_b":"(0, 1)","option_c":"(0, -1)","option_d":"(1, 0)","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Compare y^2 = 4x with y^2 = 4ax. Thus a = 1, and the focus is (1, 0).","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0018","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"ellipse","chapter_title":"Ellipse","statement":"An ellipse has semi-major axis 5 and semi-minor axis 4. Find its eccentricity.","chapter_num":16,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"3/5","option_b":"5/3","option_c":"4/5","option_d":"3/4","correct_option":"a","explanation":"c^2 = a^2 - b^2 = 9, so c = 3. Eccentricity = c/a = 3/5.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0019","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"vectors","chapter_title":"Vectors","statement":"Find the dot product of vectors (1, 2) and (2, 1).","chapter_num":17,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"5","option_b":"4","option_c":"0","option_d":"6","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Dot product = 1(2) + 2(1) = 4.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0020","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions","chapter_title":"Functions","statement":"Let f(x) = 1x + 2 and g(x) = x + 1. Find f(g(1)).","chapter_num":18,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"3","option_b":"4","option_c":"5","option_d":"2","correct_option":"b","explanation":"g(1) = 2; then f(2) = 1(2) + 2 = 4.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0021","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"complex-numbers","chapter_title":"Complex Numbers","statement":"If z = 3 + 4i, find z times its complex conjugate.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"25","option_b":"7","option_c":"-7","option_d":"24","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The conjugate is 3 - 4i. Their product is 3^2 + 4^2 = 25.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0022","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"matrices-and-determinants","chapter_title":"Matrices and Determinants","statement":"Find the determinant of the matrix with rows (3, 2) and (3, 6).","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"12","option_b":"14","option_c":"-12","option_d":"24","correct_option":"a","explanation":"For a 2 by 2 matrix, determinant = ad - bc = 3(6) - 2(3) = 12.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0023","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"quadratic-equations","chapter_title":"Quadratic Equations","statement":"What is the sum of the roots of x^2 - 6x + 8 = 0?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"-6","option_b":"6","option_c":"-8","option_d":"8","correct_option":"b","explanation":"For x^2 + bx + c = 0, root sum is -b. Here b = -6, so the sum is 6.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0024","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"An arithmetic sequence has first term 3 and common difference 2. Find its 6th term.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"12","option_b":"13","option_c":"15","option_d":"11","correct_option":"b","explanation":"a_n = a + (n - 1)d = 3 + 5(2) = 1