option_c":"5/8","option_d":"1/8","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Probability = favorable/total = 3/8 = 3/8.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0049","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"binomial-theorem","chapter_title":"Binomial Theorem","statement":"What is the coefficient of x^2 in the expansion of (1 + x)^6?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"15","option_b":"21","option_c":"6","option_d":"30","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The coefficient is 6C2 = 6(5)/2 = 15.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0050","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"trigonometry","chapter_title":"Trigonometry","statement":"For an acute angle theta, the opposite side is 8 and hypotenuse is 17. Find sin(theta).","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"17/8","option_b":"8/15","option_c":"8/17","option_d":"15/17","correct_option":"c","explanation":"sin(theta) = opposite/hypotenuse = 8/17 = 8/17.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0051","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions-and-limits","chapter_title":"Functions and Limits","statement":"Evaluate limit as x approaches 4 of (x^2 - 16)/(x - 4).","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"16","option_b":"4","option_c":"8","option_d":"9","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Factor the numerator as (x - 4)(x + 4). The limit is 4 + 4 = 8.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0052","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"differentiation","chapter_title":"Differentiation","statement":"If f(x) = x^2 + 3x, find f'(5).","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"40","option_b":"10","option_c":"13","option_d":"14","correct_option":"c","explanation":"f'(x) = 2x + 3. Thus f'(5) = 13.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0053","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"maxima-and-minima","chapter_title":"Maxima and Minima","statement":"The function f(x) = (x - 3)^2 + 6 has its minimum value at which x?","chapter_num":11,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"9","option_c":"-3","option_d":"3","correct_option":"d","explanation":"A square is smallest when x - 3 = 0, so x = 3.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0054","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"integration","chapter_title":"Integration","statement":"Evaluate the definite integral of x^3 from x = 0 to x = 1.","chapter_num":12,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"3/4","option_b":"4","option_c":"1/3","option_d":"1/4","correct_option":"d","explanation":"An antiderivative is x^4/4. Applying 0 and 1 gives 1/4.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0055","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"straight-lines","chapter_title":"Straight Lines","statement":"Find the slope of the line through (2, 3) and (4, 9).","chapter_num":13,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"3","option_b":"4","option_c":"3/2","option_d":"6","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Slope = (9 - 3)/(4 - 2) = 6/2 = 3.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0056","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"circle","chapter_title":"Circle","statement":"What is the radius of the circle x^2 + y^2 - 8x + 7 = 0?","chapter_num":14,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"9","option_b":"3","option_c":"4","option_d":"1","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Complete the square: (x - 4)^2 + y^2 = 9. Hence the radius is 3.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0057","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"parabola","chapter_title":"Parabola","statement":"The parabola y^2 = 12x has focus at which point?","chapter_num":15,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"(0, 3)","option_b":"(3, 0)","option_c":"(-3, 0)","option_d":"(0, -3)","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Compare y^2 = 12x with y^2 = 4ax. Thus a = 3, and the focus is (3, 0).","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0058","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"ellipse","chapter_title":"Ellipse","statement":"An ellipse has semi-major axis 10 and semi-minor axis 8. Find its eccentricity.","chapter_num":16,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"5/3","option_b":"3/4","option_c":"3/5","option_d":"4/5","correct_option":"c","explanation":"c^2 = a^2 - b^2 = 36, so c = 6. Eccentricity = c/a = 3/5.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0059","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"vectors","chapter_title":"Vectors","statement":"Find the dot product of vectors (3, 6) and (4, 1).","chapter_num":17,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"18","option_b":"14","option_c":"6","option_d":"22","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Dot product = 3(4) + 6(1) = 18.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0060","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions","chapter_title":"Functions","statement":"Let f(x) = 3x + 4 and g(x) = x + 1. Find f(g(7)).","chapter_num":18,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"8","option_b":"25","option_c":"28","option_d":"31","correct_option":"c","explanation":"g(7) = 8; then f(8) = 3(8) + 4 = 28.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0061","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"complex-numbers","chapter_title":"Complex Numbers","statement":"If z = 5 + 3i, find z times its complex conjugate.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"30","option_b":"16","option_c":"8","option_d":"34","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The conjugate is 5 - 3i. Their product is 5^2 + 3^2 = 34.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0062","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"matrices-and-determinants","chapter_title":"Matrices and Determinants","statement":"Find the determinant of the matrix with rows (5, 4) and (3, 5).","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"-13","option_b":"13","option_c":"17","option_d":"37","correct_option":"b","explanation":"For a 2 by 2 matrix, determinant = ad - bc = 5(5) - 4(3) = 13.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0063","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"quadratic-equations","chapter_title":"Quadratic Equations","statement":"What is the sum of the roots of x^2 - 12x + 32 = 0?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"32","option_b":"-32","option_c":"-12","option_d":"12","correct_option":"d","explanation":"For x^2 + bx + c = 0, root sum is -b. Here b = -12, so the sum is 12.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0064","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"An arithmetic sequence has first term 5 and common difference 4. Find its 8th term.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"29","option_b":"37","option_c":"33","option_d":"32","correct_option":"c","exp