"topic","option_a":"5","option_b":"8","option_c":"9","option_d":"3","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Complete the square: (x - 8)^2 + y^2 = 9. Hence the radius is 3.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0137","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"parabola","chapter_title":"Parabola","statement":"The parabola y^2 = 28x has focus at which point?","chapter_num":15,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"(0, -7)","option_b":"(7, 0)","option_c":"(-7, 0)","option_d":"(0, 7)","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Compare y^2 = 28x with y^2 = 4ax. Thus a = 7, and the focus is (7, 0).","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0138","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"ellipse","chapter_title":"Ellipse","statement":"An ellipse has semi-major axis 10 and semi-minor axis 8. Find its eccentricity.","chapter_num":16,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"5/3","option_b":"4/5","option_c":"3/4","option_d":"3/5","correct_option":"d","explanation":"c^2 = a^2 - b^2 = 36, so c = 6. Eccentricity = c/a = 3/5.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0139","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"vectors","chapter_title":"Vectors","statement":"Find the dot product of vectors (7, 7) and (3, 1).","chapter_num":17,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"14","option_b":"28","option_c":"52","option_d":"18","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Dot product = 7(3) + 7(1) = 28.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0140","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions","chapter_title":"Functions","statement":"Let f(x) = 7x + 2 and g(x) = x + 1. Find f(g(3)).","chapter_num":18,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"30","option_b":"37","option_c":"23","option_d":"4","correct_option":"a","explanation":"g(3) = 4; then f(4) = 7(4) + 2 = 30.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0141","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"complex-numbers","chapter_title":"Complex Numbers","statement":"If z = 9 + 1i, find z times its complex conjugate.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"10","option_b":"82","option_c":"80","option_d":"18","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The conjugate is 9 - 1i. Their product is 9^2 + 1^2 = 82.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0142","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"matrices-and-determinants","chapter_title":"Matrices and Determinants","statement":"Find the determinant of the matrix with rows (2, 3) and (3, 3).","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"3","option_b":"11","option_c":"15","option_d":"-3","correct_option":"d","explanation":"For a 2 by 2 matrix, determinant = ad - bc = 2(3) - 3(3) = -3.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0143","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"quadratic-equations","chapter_title":"Quadratic Equations","statement":"What is the sum of the roots of x^2 - 15x + 56 = 0?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"-56","option_b":"-15","option_c":"56","option_d":"15","correct_option":"d","explanation":"For x^2 + bx + c = 0, root sum is -b. Here b = -15, so the sum is 15.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0144","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"An arithmetic sequence has first term 9 and common difference 2. Find its 12th term.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"29","option_b":"33","option_c":"31","option_d":"24","correct_option":"c","explanation":"a_n = a + (n - 1)d = 9 + 11(2) = 31.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0145","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"Find the sum of the first three terms of the geometric sequence with first term 3 and ratio 3.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"39","option_b":"27","option_c":"12","option_d":"40","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The terms are 3, 9, and 27; their sum is 39.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0146","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many ordered arrangements of 2 objects can be selected from 11 distinct objects?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"110","option_b":"55","option_c":"22","option_d":"121","correct_option":"a","explanation":"This is 11P2 = 11(10) = 110.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0147","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many unordered pairs can be chosen from 12 distinct students?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"132","option_b":"14","option_c":"66","option_d":"24","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The count is 12C2 = 12(11)/2 = 66.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0148","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"probability","chapter_title":"Probability","st