":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"differentiation","chapter_title":"Differentiation","statement":"If f(x) = x^2 + 1x, find f'(3).","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"7","option_c":"8","option_d":"12","correct_option":"b","explanation":"f'(x) = 2x + 1. Thus f'(3) = 7.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0173","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"maxima-and-minima","chapter_title":"Maxima and Minima","statement":"The function f(x) = (x - 9)^2 + 2 has its minimum value at which x?","chapter_num":11,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"9","option_b":"11","option_c":"-9","option_d":"2","correct_option":"a","explanation":"A square is smallest when x - 9 = 0, so x = 9.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0174","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"integration","chapter_title":"Integration","statement":"Evaluate the definite integral of x^1 from x = 0 to x = 1.","chapter_num":12,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"1","option_b":"1/2","option_c":"2","option_d":"3/2","correct_option":"b","explanation":"An antiderivative is x^2/2. Applying 0 and 1 gives 1/2.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0175","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"straight-lines","chapter_title":"Straight Lines","statement":"Find the slope of the line through (3, 3) and (5, 7).","chapter_num":13,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"4","option_b":"2","option_c":"3","option_d":"1","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Slope = (7 - 3)/(5 - 3) = 4/2 = 2.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0176","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapte