itle":"Functions","statement":"Let f(x) = 2x + 4 and g(x) = x + 1. Find f(g(1)).","chapter_num":18,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"8","option_c":"2","option_d":"10","correct_option":"b","explanation":"g(1) = 2; then f(2) = 2(2) + 4 = 8.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0181","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"complex-numbers","chapter_title":"Complex Numbers","statement":"If z = 3 + 7i, find z times its complex conjugate.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"58","option_b":"10","option_c":"-40","option_d":"42","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The conjugate is 3 - 7i. Their product is 3^2 + 7^2 = 58.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0182","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"matrices-and-determinants","chapter_title":"Matrices and Determinants","statement":"Find the determinant of the matrix with rows (4, 5) and (3, 9).","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"21","option_b":"22","option_c":"51","option_d":"-21","correct_option":"a","explanation":"For a 2 by 2 matrix, determinant = ad - bc = 4(9) - 5(3) = 21.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0183","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"quadratic-equations","chapter_title":"Quadratic Equations","statement":"What is the sum of the roots of x^2 - 4x + 4 = 0?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"-4","option_c":"4","option_d":"5","correct_option":"c","explanation":"For x^2 + bx + c = 0, root sum is -b. Here b = -4, so the sum is 4.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0184","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"An arithmetic sequence has first term 2 and common difference 4. Find its 6th term.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"22","option_b":"24","option_c":"26","option_d":"18","correct_option":"a","explanation":"a_n = a + (n - 1)d = 2 + 5(4) = 22.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0185","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"Find the sum of the first three terms of the geometric sequence with first term 5 and ratio 2.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"15","option_b":"30","option_c":"35","option_d":"20","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The terms are 5, 10, and 20; their sum is 35.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0186","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many ordered arrangements of 2 objects can be selected from 5 distinct objects?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"20","option_b":"25","option_c":"21","option_d":"10","correct_option":"a","explanation":"This is 5P2 = 5(4) = 20.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0187","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many unordered pairs can be chosen from 5 distinct students?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"10","option_b":"7","option_c":"11","option_d":"20","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The count is 5C2 = 5(4)/2 = 10.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0188","subjec