"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0192","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"differentiation","chapter_title":"Differentiation","statement":"If f(x) = x^2 + 2x, find f'(5).","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"12","option_b":"35","option_c":"13","option_d":"10","correct_option":"a","explanation":"f'(x) = 2x + 2. Thus f'(5) = 12.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0193","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"maxima-and-minima","chapter_title":"Maxima and Minima","statement":"The function f(x) = (x - 1)^2 + 4 has its minimum value at which x?","chapter_num":11,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"4","option_b":"1","option_c":"-1","option_d":"5","correct_option":"b","explanation":"A square is smallest when x - 1 = 0, so x = 1.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0194","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"integration","chapter_title":"Integration","statement":"Evaluate the definite integral of x^2 from x = 0 to x = 1.","chapter_num":12,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"3","option_b":"2/3","option_c":"1/2","option_d":"1/3","correct_option":"d","explanation":"An antiderivative is x^3/3. Applying 0 and 1 gives 1/3.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0195","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"straight-lines","chapter_title":"Straight Lines","statement":"Find the slope of the line through (4, 4) and (6, 10).","chapter_num":13,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"3/2","option_b":"4","option_c":"6","option_d":"3","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Slope = (10 - 4)/(6 - 4) = 6/2 = 3.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0196","subject":"Advanced 