6","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"circle","chapter_title":"Circle","statement":"What is the radius of the circle x^2 + y^2 - 4x + -5 = 0?","chapter_num":14,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"9","option_b":"1","option_c":"2","option_d":"3","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Complete the square: (x - 2)^2 + y^2 = 9. Hence the radius is 3.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0217","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"parabola","chapter_title":"Parabola","statement":"The parabola y^2 = 8x has focus at which point?","chapter_num":15,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"(-2, 0)","option_b":"(2, 0)","option_c":"(0, 2)","option_d":"(0, -2)","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Compare y^2 = 8x with y^2 = 4ax. Thus a = 2, and the focus is (2, 0).","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0218","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"ellipse","chapter_title":"Ellipse","statement":"An ellipse has semi-major axis 10 and semi-minor axis 8. Find its eccentricity.","chapter_num":16,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"3/5","option_b":"3/4","option_c":"4/5","option_d":"5/3","correct_option":"a","explanation":"c^2 = a^2 - b^2 = 36, so c = 6. Eccentricity = c/a = 3/5.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0219","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"vectors","chapter_title":"Vectors","statement":"Find the dot product of vectors (4, 8) and (2, 1).","chapter_num":17,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"34","option_b":"0","option_c":"16","option_d":"15","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Dot product = 4(2) + 8(1) = 16.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0220","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions","chapter_title":"Functions","statement":"Let f(x) = 4x + 6 and g(x) = x + 1. Find f(g(7)).","chapter_num":18,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"8","option_b":"34","option_c":"38","option_d":"42","correct_option":"c","explanation":"g(7) = 8; then f(8) = 4(8) + 6 = 38.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0221","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"complex-numbers","chapter_title":"Complex Numbers","statement":"If z = 5 + 6i, find z times its complex conjugate.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"60","option_b":"61","option_c":"-11","option_d":"11","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The conjugate is 5 - 6i. Their product is 5^2 + 6^2 = 61.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0222","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"matrices-and-determinants","chapter_title":"Matrices and Determinants","statement":"Find the determinant of the matrix with rows (6, 2) and (3, 8).","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"54","option_b":"19","option_c":"-42","option_d":"42","correct_option":"d","explanation":"For a 2 by 2 matrix, determinant = ad - bc = 6(8) - 2(3) = 42.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0223","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"quadratic-equations","chapter_title":"Quadratic Equations","statement":"What is the sum of the roots of x^2 - 10x + 24 = 0?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"-24","option_b":"-10","option_c":"10","option_d":"24","correct_option":"c","explanation":"For x^2 + bx + c = 0, root sum is -b. Here b = -10, so the sum is 10.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0224","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"An arithmetic sequence has first term 4 and common difference 6. Find its 8th term.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"40","option_b":"52","option_c":"46","option_d":"48","correct_option":"c","explanation":"a_n = a + (n - 1)d = 4 + 7(6) = 46.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0225","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"Find the sum of the first three terms of the geometric sequence with first term 2 and ratio 4.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"42","option_b":"24","option_c":"10","option_d":"32","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The terms are 2, 8, and 32; their sum is 42.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0226","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many ordered arrangements of 2 objects can be selected from 7 distinct objects?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"42","option_b":"21","option_c":"49","option_d":"14","correct_option":"a","explanation":"This is 7P2 = 7(6) = 42.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0227","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many unordered pairs can be chosen from 7 distinct students?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"14","option_b":"42","option_c":"21","option_d":"9","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The count is 7C2 = 7(6)/2 = 21.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0228","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"probability","chapter_title":"Probability","statement":"A box has 10 equally likely numbered slips, of which 3 are marked. What is the probability of drawing a marked slip?","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"7/10","option_b":"3/10","option_c":"3/11","option_d":"1/10","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Probability = favorable/total = 3/10 = 3/10.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0229","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"binomial-theorem","chapter_title":"Binomial Theorem","statement":"What is the coefficient of x^2 in the expansion of (1 + x)^6?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"15","option_c":"30","option_d":"21","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The coefficient is 6C2 = 6(5)/2 = 15.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0230","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"trigonometry","chapter_title":"Trigonometry","statement":"For an acute angle theta, the opposite side is 7 and hypotenuse is 25. Find sin(theta).","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"25/7","option_b":"7/24","option_c":"7/25","option_d":"24/25","correct_option":"c","explanation":"sin(theta) = opposite/hypotenuse = 7/25 = 7/25.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0231","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions-and-limits","chapter_title":"Functions and Limits","statement":"Evaluate limit as x approaches 13 of (x^2 - 169)/(x - 13).","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"169","option_b":"27","option_c":"26","option_d":"13","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Factor the numerator as (x - 13)(x + 13). The limit is 13 + 13 = 26.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0232","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"differentiation","chapter_title":"Differentiation","statement":"If f(x) = x^2 + 4x, find f'(2).","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"8","option_b":"12","option_c":"4","option_d":"9","correct_option":"a","explanation":"f'(x) = 2x + 4. Thus f'(2) = 8.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0233","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"maxima-and-minima","chapter_title":"Maxima and Minima","statement":"The function f(x) = (x - 3)^2 + 8 has its minimum value at which x?","chapter_num":11,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"-3","option_b":"3","option_c":"11","option_d":"8","correct_option":"b","explanation":"A square is smallest when x - 3 = 0, so x = 3.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0234","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"integration","chapter_title":"Integration","statement":"Evaluate the definite integral of x^4 from x = 0 to x = 1.","chapter_num":12,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"5","option_b":"4/5","option_c":"1/4","option_d":"1/5","correct_option":"d","explanation":"An antiderivative is x^5/5. Applying 0 and 1 gives 1/5.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0235","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"straight-lines","chapter_title":"Straight Lines","statement":"Find the slope of the line through (1, 6) and (3, 16).","chapter_num":13,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"5","option_b":"5/2","option_c":"6","option_d":"10","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Slope = (16 - 6)/(3 - 1) = 10/2 = 5.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0236","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"circle","chapter_title":"Circle","statement":"What is the radius of the circle x^2 + y^2 - 6x + 0 = 0?","chapter_num":14,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"0","option_b":"3","option_c":"4","option_d":"9","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Complete the square: (x - 3)^2 + y^2 = 9. Hence the radius is 3.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0237","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"parabola","chapter_title":"Parabola","statement":"The parabola y^2 = 12x has focus at which point?","chapter_num":15,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"(0, -3)","option_b":"(0, 3)","option_c":"(3, 0)","option_d":"(-3, 0)","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Compare y^2 = 12x with y^2 = 4ax. Thus a = 3, and the focus is (3, 0).","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0238","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"ellipse","chapter_title":"Ellipse","statement":"An ellipse has semi-major axis 17 and semi-minor axis 15. Find its eccentricity.","chapter_num":16,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"8/17","option_b":"17/8","option_c":"15/17","option_d":"8/15","correct_option":"a","explanation":"c^2 = a^2 - b^2 = 64, so c = 8. Eccentricity = c/a = 8/17.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0239","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"vectors","chapter_title":"Vectors","statement":"Find the dot product of vectors (5, 3) and (3, 4).","chapter_num":17,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"27","option_b":"3","option_c":"28","option_d":"15","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Dot product = 5(3) + 3(4) = 27.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-s