5).","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"15","option_b":"30","option_c":"31","option_d":"225","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Factor the numerator as (x - 15)(x + 15). The limit is 15 + 15 = 30.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0272","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"differentiation","chapter_title":"Differentiation","statement":"If f(x) = x^2 + 6x, find f'(6).","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"72","option_b":"18","option_c":"19","option_d":"12","correct_option":"b","explanation":"f'(x) = 2x + 6. Thus f'(6) = 18.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0273","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"maxima-and-minima","chapter_title":"Maxima and Minima","statement":"The function f(x) = (x - 5)^2 + 4 has its minimum value at which x?","chapter_num":11,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"9","option_b":"5","option_c":"-5","option_d":"4","correct_option":"b","explanation":"A square is smallest when x - 5 = 0, so x = 5.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0274","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"integration","chapter_title":"Integration","statement":"Evaluate the definite integral of x^6 from x = 0 to x = 1.","chapter_num":12,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"1/6","option_b":"6/7","option_c":"7","option_d":"1/7","correct_option":"d","explanation":"An antiderivative is x^7/7. Applying 0 and 1 gives 1/7.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0275","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"straight-lines","chapter_title":"Straight Lines","statement":"Find the slope of the line through (3, 2) and (5, 16).","chapter_num":13,"node_kind":"topic","optio