limits","chapter_title":"Functions and Limits","statement":"Evaluate limit as x approaches 2 of (x^2 - 4)/(x - 2).","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"4","option_c":"2","option_d":"5","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Factor the numerator as (x - 2)(x + 2). The limit is 2 + 2 = 4.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0312","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"differentiation","chapter_title":"Differentiation","statement":"If f(x) = x^2 + 8x, find f'(3).","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"14","option_b":"6","option_c":"33","option_d":"15","correct_option":"a","explanation":"f'(x) = 2x + 8. Thus f'(3) = 14.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0313","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"maxima-and-minima","chapter_title":"Maxima and Minima","statement":"The function f(x) = (x - 7)^2 + 8 has its minimum value at which x?","chapter_num":11,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"-7","option_b":"8","option_c":"15","option_d":"7","correct_option":"d","explanation":"A square is smallest when x - 7 = 0, so x = 7.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0314","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"integration","chapter_title":"Integration","statement":"Evaluate the definite integral of x^8 from x = 0 to x = 1.","chapter_num":12,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"1/8","option_b":"1/9","option_c":"8/9","option_d":"9","correct_option":"b","explanation":"An antiderivative is x^9/9. Applying 0 and 1 gives 1/9.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0315","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"straight-lines","chapter_title":"Straight Lines","statem