matics","chapter_slug":"straight-lines","chapter_title":"Straight Lines","statement":"Find the slope of the line through (2, 6) and (4, 14).","chapter_num":13,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"8","option_b":"2","option_c":"5","option_d":"4","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Slope = (14 - 6)/(4 - 2) = 8/2 = 4.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0356","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"circle","chapter_title":"Circle","statement":"What is the radius of the circle x^2 + y^2 - 18x + 72 = 0?","chapter_num":14,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"9","option_b":"6","option_c":"4","option_d":"3","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Complete the square: (x - 9)^2 + y^2 = 9. Hence the radius is 3.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0357","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"parabola","chapter_title":"Parabola","statement":"The parabola y^2 = 36x has focus at which point?","chapter_num":15,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"(0, 9)","option_b":"(-9, 0)","option_c":"(0, -9)","option_d":"(9, 0)","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Compare y^2 = 36x with y^2 = 4ax. Thus a = 9, and the focus is (9, 0).","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0358","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"ellipse","chapter_title":"Ellipse","statement":"An ellipse has semi-major axis 13 and semi-minor axis 12. Find its eccentricity.","chapter_num":16,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"12/13","option_b":"5/12","option_c":"5/13","option_d":"13/5","correct_option":"c","explanation":"c^2 = a^2 - b^2 = 25, so c = 5. Eccentricity = c/a = 5/13.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0359","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"vectors","chapter_title":"Vectors","statement":"Find the dot product of vectors (4, 8) and (4, 4).","chapter_num":17,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"48","option_b":"49","option_c":"-16","option_d":"20","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Dot product = 4(4) + 8(4) = 48.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0360","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions","chapter_title":"Functions","statement":"Let f(x) = 4x + 7 and g(x) = x + 1. Find f(g(4)).","chapter_num":18,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"23","option_b":"27","option_c":"31","option_d":"5","correct_option":"b","explanation":"g(4) = 5; then f(5) = 4(5) + 7 = 27.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0361","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"complex-numbers","chapter_title":"Complex Numbers","statement":"If z = 4 + 6i, find z times its complex conjugate.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"48","option_b":"-20","option_c":"52","option_d":"10","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The conjugate is 4 - 6i. Their product is 4^2 + 6^2 = 52.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0362","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"matrices-and-determinants","chapter_title":"Matrices and Determinants","statement":"Find the determinant of the matrix with rows (6, 4) and (1, 8).","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"-44","option_b":"19","option_c":"52","option_d":"44","correct_option":"d","explanation":"For a 2 by 2 matrix, determinant = ad - bc = 6(8) - 4(1) = 44.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0363","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"quadratic-equations","chapter_title":"Quadratic Equations","statement":"What is the sum of the roots of x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"5","option_c":"-6","option_d":"-5","correct_option":"b","explanation":"For x^2 + bx + c = 0, root sum is -b. Here b = -5, so the sum is 5.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0364","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"An arithmetic sequence has first term 2 and common difference 1. Find its 7th term.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"9","option_b":"7","option_c":"8","option_d":"10","correct_option":"c","explanation":"a_n = a + (n - 1)d = 2 + 6(1) = 8.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0365","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"Find the sum of the first three terms of the geometric sequence with first term 4 and ratio 2.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"12","option_b":"16","option_c":"24","option_d":"28","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The terms are 4, 8, and 16; their sum is 28.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0366","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many ordered arrangements of 2 objects can be selected from 6 distinct objects?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"30","option_b":"15","option_c":"12","option_d":"36","correct_option":"a","explanation":"This is 6P2 = 6(5) = 30.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0367","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advan