:"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0391","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions-and-limits","chapter_title":"Functions and Limits","statement":"Evaluate limit as x approaches 6 of (x^2 - 36)/(x - 6).","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"12","option_b":"36","option_c":"6","option_d":"13","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Factor the numerator as (x - 6)(x + 6). The limit is 6 + 6 = 12.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0392","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"differentiation","chapter_title":"Differentiation","statement":"If f(x) = x^2 + 4x, find f'(4).","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"32","option_b":"13","option_c":"8","option_d":"12","correct_option":"d","explanation":"f'(x) = 2x + 4. Thus f'(4) = 12.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0393","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"maxima-and-minima","chapter_title":"Maxima and Minima","statement":"The function f(x) = (x - 2)^2 + 8 has its minimum value at which x?","chapter_num":11,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"10","option_b":"-2","option_c":"2","option_d":"8","correct_option":"c","explanation":"A square is smallest when x - 2 = 0, so x = 2.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0394","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"integration","chapter_title":"Integration","statement":"Evaluate the definite integral of x^4 from x = 0 to x = 1.","chapter_num":12,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"5","option_b":"4/5","option_c":"1/5","option_d":"1/4","correct_option":"c","explanation":"An antiderivative is x^5/5. Applying 0 and 1 gives 1/5.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0395","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"straight-lines","chapter_title":"Straight Lines","statement":"Find the slope of the line through (4, 2) and (6, 14).","chapter_num":13,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"12","option_c":"7","option_d":"3","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Slope = (14 - 2)/(6 - 4) = 12/2 = 6.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0396","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"circle","chapter_title":"Circle","statement":"What is the radius of the circle x^2 + y^2 - 22x + 112 = 0?","chapter_num":14,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"3","option_b":"11","option_c":"9","option_d":"8","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Complete the square: (x - 11)^2 + y^2 = 9. Hence the radius is 3.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0397","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"parabola","chapter_title":"Parabola","statement":"The parabola y^2 = 8x has focus at which point?","chapter_num":15,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"(0, 2)","option_b":"(2, 0)","option_c":"(0, -2)","option_d":"(-2, 0)","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Compare y^2 = 8x with y^2 = 4ax. Thus a = 2, and the focus is (2, 0).","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0398","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"ellipse","chapter_title":"Ellipse","statement":"An ellipse has semi-major axis 17 and semi-minor axis 15. Find its eccentricity.","chapter_num":16,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"8/17","option_b":"15/17","option_c":"8/15","option_d":"17/8","correct_option":"a","explanation":"c^2 = a^2 - b^2 = 64, so c = 8. Eccentricity = c/a = 8/17.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0399","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"vectors","chapter_title":"Vectors","statement":"Find the dot product of vectors (6, 5) and (6, 4).","chapter_num":17,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"16","option_b":"54","option_c":"56","option_d":"21","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Dot product = 6(6) + 5(4) = 56.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0400","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions","chapter_title":"Functions","statement":"Let f(x) = 6x + 3 and g(x) = x + 1. Find f(g(2)).","chapter_num":18,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"27","option_b":"21","option_c":"3","option_d":"15","correct_option":"b","explanation":"g(2) = 3; then f(3) = 6(3) + 3 = 21.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0401","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"complex-numbers","chapter_title":"Complex Numbers","statement":"If z = 6 + 5i, find z times its complex conjugate.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"11","option_b":"62","option_c":"60","option_d":"61","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The conjugate is 6 - 5i. Their product is 6^2 + 5^2 = 61.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0402","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"matrices-and-determinants","chapter_title":"Matrices and Determinants","statement":"Find the determinant of the matrix with rows (8, 1) and (1, 7).","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"-55","option_b":"57","option_c":"17","option_d":"55","correct_option":"d","explanation":"For a 2 by 2 matrix, determinant = ad - bc = 8(7) - 1(1) = 55.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0403","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"quadratic-equations","chapter_title":"Quadratic Equations","statement":"What is the sum of the roots of x^2 - 11x + 30 = 0?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"11","option_b":"-11","option_c":"-30","option_d":"30","correct_option":"a","explanation":"For x^2 + bx + c = 0, root sum is -b. Here b = -11, so the sum is 11.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0404","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"An arithmetic sequence has first term 4 and common difference 3. Find its 9th term.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"31","option_b":"25","option_c":"28","option_d":"27","correct_option":"c","explanation":"a_n = a + (n - 1)d = 4 + 8(3) = 28.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0405","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"sequences-and-series","chapter_title":"Sequences and Series","statement":"Find the sum of the first three terms of the geometric sequence with first term 1 and ratio 4.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"5","option_b":"21","option_c":"16","option_d":"12","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The terms are 1, 4, and 16; their sum is 21.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0406","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many ordered arrangements of 2 objects can be selected from 8 distinct objects?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"16","option_b":"64","option_c":"56","option_d":"28","correct_option":"c","explanation":"This is 8P2 = 8(7) = 56.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0407","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"permutations-and-combinations","chapter_title":"Permutations and Combinations","statement":"How many unordered pairs can be chosen from 7 distinct students?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"9","option_b":"21","option_c":"14","option_d":"42","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The count is 7C2 = 7(6)/2 = 21.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0408","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"probability","chapter_title":"Probability","statement":"A box has 12 equally likely numbered slips, of which 10 are marked. What is the probability of drawing a marked slip?","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"10/13","option_b":"1/12","option_c":"1/6","option_d":"5/6","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Probability = favorable/total = 10/12 = 5/6.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0409","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"binomial-theorem","chapter_title":"Binomial Theorem","statement":"What is the coefficient of x^2 in the expansion of (1 + x)^6?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"15","option_b":"6","option_c":"21","option_d":"30","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The coefficient is 6C2 = 6(5)/2 = 15.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0410","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"trigonometry","chapter_title":"Trigonometry","statement":"For an acute angle theta, the opposite side is 3 and hypotenuse is 5. Find sin(theta).","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"5/3","option_b":"4/5","option_c":"3/4","option_d":"3/5","correct_option":"d","explanation":"sin(theta) = opposite/hypotenuse = 3/5 = 3/5.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0411","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"functions-and-limits","chapter_title":"Functions and Limits","statement":"Evaluate limit as x approaches 7 of (x^2 - 49)/(x - 7).","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"15","option_b":"7","option_c":"14","option_d":"49","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Factor the numerator as (x - 7)(x + 7). The limit is 7 + 7 = 14.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0412","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"differentiation","chapter_title":"Differentiation","statement":"If f(x) = x^2 + 5x, find f'(6).","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"12","option_b":"18","option_c":"17","option_d":"66","correct_option":"c","explanation":"f'(x) = 2x + 5. Thus f'(6) = 17.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0413","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"maxima-and-minima","chapter_title":"Maxima and Minima","statement":"The function f(x) = (x - 3)^2 + 2 has its minimum value at which x?","chapter_num":11,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"2","option_b":"5","option_c":"-3","option_d":"3","correct_option":"d","explanation":"A square is smallest when x - 3 = 0, so x = 3.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0414","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"integration","chapter_title":"Integration","statement":"Evaluate the definite integral of x^5 from x = 0 to x = 1.","chapter_num":12,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6","option_b":"1/5","option_c":"1/6","option_d":"5/6","correct_option":"c","explanation":"An antiderivative is x^6/6. Applying 0 and 1 gives 1/6.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0415","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"straight-lines","chapter_title":"Straight Lines","statement":"Find the slope of the line through (0, 3) and (2, 17).","chapter_num":13,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"8","option_b":"14","option_c":"7","option_d":"7/2","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Slope = (17 - 3)/(2 - 0) = 14/2 = 7.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0416","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"circle","chapter_title":"Circle","statement":"What is the radius of the circle x^2 + y^2 - 4x + -5 = 0?","chapter_num":14,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"1","option_b":"2","option_c":"3","option_d":"9","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Complete the square: (x - 2)^2 + y^2 = 9. Hence the radius is 3.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0417","subject":"Advanced Mathematics","subject_slug":"advanced-mathematics","chapter_slug":"parabola","chapter_title":"Parabola","statement":"The parabola y^2 = 12x has focus at which point?","chapter_num":15,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"(0, 3)","option_b":"(-3, 0)","option_c":"(0, -3)","option_d":"(3, 0)","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Compare y^2 = 12x with y^2 = 4ax. Thus a = 3, and the focus is (3, 0).","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0418","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"percentages","chapter_title":"Percentages","statement":"What is 10 percent of 20?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"30","option_b":"2","option_c":"18","option_d":"200","correct_option":"b","explanation":"10 percent of 20 = 10/100 times 20 = 2.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0419","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"ratios-and-proportions","chapter_title":"Ratios and Proportions","statement":"Two quantities are in the ratio 2:3. If the first is 4, what is the second?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"2","option_b":"6","option_c":"7","option_d":"9","correct_option":"b","explanation":"One ratio unit is 4/2 = 2; the second is 3(2) = 6.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0420","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"profit-and-loss","chapter_title":"Profit and Loss","statement":"An item costing Rs 100 is sold at a 10 percent profit. Find the selling price.","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"90","option_b":"10","option_c":"110","option_d":"111","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Profit = 10 percent of 100 = 10. Selling price = 100 + 10 = 110.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0421","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"simple-interest","chapter_title":"Simple Interest","statement":"Find the simple interest on Rs 1000 at 5 percent per year for 2 years.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"50","option_b":"1100","option_c":"100","option_d":"102","correct_option":"c","explanation":"SI = PRT/100 = 1000(5)(2)/100 = 100.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0422","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"compound-interest","chapter_title":"Compound Interest","statement":"Rs 200 is invested at 10 percent compound interest annually for 2 years. Find the amount.","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"243","option_b":"240","option_c":"242","option_d":"220","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Amount = 200(1.1)^2 = 200 times 1.21 = 242.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0423","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"work-and-time","chapter_title":"Work and Time","statement":"One worker finishes a job in 2 days and another in 3 days. How many days do they need together?","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6/5","option_b":"5","option_c":"5/6","option_d":"2","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Combined rate = 1/2 + 1/3 = 5/6; time is its reciprocal, 6/5 days.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0424","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"age-problems","chapter_title":"Age Problems","statement":"Ali is 10 years old and Sara is 3 years older. How old will Sara be after 2 years?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"13","option_b":"5","option_c":"15","option_d":"12","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Sara is now 10+3 = 13; after 2 years she will be 15.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0425","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"distance-speed-and-time","chapter_title":"Distance Speed and Time","statement":"A car travels at 30 km/h for 2 hours. What distance does it cover?","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"32","option_b":"15","option_c":"90","option_d":"60","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Distance = speed times time = 30(2) = 60 km.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0426","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"linear-inequalities","chapter_title":"Linear Inequalities","statement":"Solve the inequality 2x + 3 < 13.","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"x < 10","option_b":"x > 5","option_c":"x < 5","option_d":"x > 10","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Subtract 3: 2x < 10. Divide by positive 2: x < 5.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0427","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"mensuration","chapter_title":"Mensuration","statement":"Find the area of a rectangle of length 4 cm and width 3 cm.","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"14","option_b":"12","option_c":"7","option_d":"24","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Area = length times width = 4(3) = 12 square cm.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0428","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"mensuration","chapter_title":"Mensuration","statement":"A cylinder has radius 2 cm and height 3 cm. Express its volume as a multiple of pi.","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"12pi","option_b":"6pi","option_c":"13pi","option_d":"7pi","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Volume = pi r^2 h = pi(2^2)(3) = 12pi cubic cm.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0429","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"percentages","chapter_title":"Percentages","statement":"A marked price is Rs 50. After a 10 percent discount, what is the sale price?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"45","option_b":"40","option_c":"5","option_d":"60","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Sale price = 90 percent of 50 = 45.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0430","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"percentages","chapter_title":"Percentages","statement":"What is 20 percent of 30?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"600","option_b":"6","option_c":"24","option_d":"50","correct_option":"b","explanation":"20 percent of 30 = 20/100 times 30 = 6.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0431","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"ratios-and-proportions","chapter_title":"Ratios and Proportions","statement":"Two quantities are in the ratio 3:5. If the first is 9, what is the second?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"3","option_b":"20","option_c":"14","option_d":"15","correct_option":"d","explanation":"One ratio unit is 9/3 = 3; the second is 5(3) = 15.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0432","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"profit-and-loss","chapter_title":"Profit and Loss","statement":"An item costing Rs 120 is sold at a 20 percent profit. Find the selling price.","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"24","option_b":"144","option_c":"96","option_d":"140","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Profit = 20 percent of 120 = 24. Selling price = 120 + 24 = 144.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0433","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"simple-interest","chapter_title":"Simple Interest","statement":"Find the simple interest on Rs 1500 at 10 percent per year for 3 years.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"450","option_b":"150","option_c":"1950","option_d":"453","correct_option":"a","explanation":"SI = PRT/100 = 1500(10)(3)/100 = 450.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0434","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"compound-interest","chapter_title":"Compound Interest","statement":"Rs 300 is invested at 10 percent compound interest annually for 2 years. Find the amount.","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"320","option_b":"330","option_c":"363","option_d":"360","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Amount = 300(1.1)^2 = 300 times 1.21 = 363.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usa