"correct_option":"a","explanation":"Sale price = 90 percent of 70 = 63.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0574","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"percentages","chapter_title":"Percentages","statement":"What is 40 percent of 30?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"1200","option_b":"12","option_c":"18","option_d":"70","correct_option":"b","explanation":"40 percent of 30 = 40/100 times 30 = 12.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0575","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"ratios-and-proportions","chapter_title":"Ratios and Proportions","statement":"Two quantities are in the ratio 3:8. If the first is 21, what is the second?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"29","option_b":"7","option_c":"56","option_d":"64","correct_option":"c","explanation":"One ratio unit is 21/3 = 7; the second is 8(7) = 56.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0576","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"profit-and-loss","chapter_title":"Profit and Loss","statement":"An item costing Rs 160 is sold at a 20 percent profit. Find the selling price.","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"32","option_b":"128","option_c":"180","option_d":"192","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Profit = 20 percent of 160 = 32. Selling price = 160 + 32 = 192.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0577","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"simple-interest","chapter_title":"Simple Interest","statement":"Find the simple interest on Rs 3500 at 10 percent per year for 3 years.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"1053","option_b":"4550","option_c":"350","option_d":"1050","correct_option":"d","explan