ic","option_a":"540","option_b":"95","option_c":"450","option_d":"18","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Distance = speed times time = 90(5) = 450 km.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0582","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"linear-inequalities","chapter_title":"Linear Inequalities","statement":"Solve the inequality 3x + 8 < 41.","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"x < 11","option_b":"x > 11","option_c":"x > 33","option_d":"x < 33","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Subtract 8: 3x < 33. Divide by positive 3: x < 11.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0583","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"mensuration","chapter_title":"Mensuration","statement":"Find the area of a rectangle of length 9 cm and width 8 cm.","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"34","option_b":"17","option_c":"144","option_d":"72","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Area = length times width = 9(8) = 72 square cm.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0584","subject":"Basic Mathematics","subject_slug":"basic-mathematics","chapter_slug":"mensuration","chapter_title":"Mensuration","statement":"A cylinder has radius 3 cm and height 8 cm. Express its volume as a multiple of pi.","chapter_num":10,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"72pi","option_b":"24pi","option_c":"48pi","option_d":"17pi","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Volume = pi r^2 h = pi(3^2)(8) = 72pi cubic cm.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0585","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 2, 4, 6, 8, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"10","option_b":"9","option_c":"12","option_d":"16","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Each term increases by 2, so the next is 8 + 2 = 10.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0586","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 1, 2, 4, 8, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"16","option_b":"10","option_c":"18","option_d":"24","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Each term is doubled, so the next is 8 times 2 = 16.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0587","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"coding-and-decoding","chapter_title":"Coding and Decoding","statement":"In a code, FAST becomes GBTU by shifting each letter 1 place(s) forward. How is MATH coded?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"NBUI","option_b":"IUBN","option_c":"LZSG","option_d":"MATH","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Shift every letter of MATH forward by 1; this gives NBUI.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0588","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"direction-sense","chapter_title":"Direction Sense","statement":"A person walks 2 km north, 3 km east, then 1 km south. Where is the person relative to the start?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"6 km north","option_b":"3 east and 1 north","option_c":"3 west and 1 north","option_d":"1 east and 3 north","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Net east displacement is 3. Net north displacement is 2 - 1 = 1; therefore the position is 3 east and 1 north.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0589","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"blood-relations","chapter_title":"Blood Relations","statement":"Amina is the mother of Bilal. Bilal is the brother of Cyrus. How is Amina related to Cyrus?","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Aunt","option_b":"Sister","option_c":"Daughter","option_d":"Mother","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Bilal and Cyrus are siblings, and Amina is Bilal's mother. Therefore Amina is also Cyrus's mother.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0590","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"linear-seating","chapter_title":"Linear Seating","statement":"Five students sit in a row. Ali is left of Bina, Bina is left of Dani, Dani is left of Esha, and Esha is left of Fari. Who sits in the middle?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Fari","option_b":"Ali","option_c":"Dani","option_d":"Bina","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The constraints fix the order as Ali, Bina, Dani, Esha, Fari. The third, or middle, student is Dani.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0591","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"scheduling","chapter_title":"Scheduling","statement":"A test is scheduled one day after Monday. On which day is it scheduled?","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Tuesday","option_b":"Thursday","option_c":"Monday","option_d":"Wednesday","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The day immediately after Monday is Tuesday.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0592","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"verbal-analogy","chapter_title":"Verbal Analogy","statement":"Complete the analogy: Book is to Read as Food is to ?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Read","option_b":"Food","option_c":"Eat","option_d":"Book","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The relationship in Book:Read is the same as in Food:Eat.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0593","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"letter-series","chapter_title":"Letter Series","statement":"Find the next letter: A, C, E, G, ?","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"A","option_b":"Insufficient information","option_c":"I","option_d":"H","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Letter positions increase by 2 each time, wrapping after Z; the next letter is I.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0594","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"circular-seating","chapter_title":"Circular Seating","statement":"Four people A, B, C, and D sit around a circular table facing the center in that clockwise order, starting with A. Who sits opposite A?","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"B","option_b":"D","option_c":"C","option_d":"A","correct_option":"c","explanation":"With four equally spaced seats, the person two positions away is opposite. That person is C.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0595","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 3, 7, 11, 15, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"30","option_b":"18","option_c":"19","option_d":"23","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Each term increases by 4, so the next is 15 + 4 = 19.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0596","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 2, 4, 8, 16, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"18","option_b":"34","option_c":"32","option_d":"48","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Each term is doubled, so the next is 16 times 2 = 32.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0597","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"coding-and-decoding","chapter_title":"Coding and Decoding","statement":"In a code, CODE becomes EQFG by shifting each letter 2 place(s) forward. How is TEST coded?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"VUGV","option_b":"VGUV","option_c":"TEST","option_d":"RCQR","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Shift every letter of TEST forward by 2; this gives VGUV.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0598","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"direction-sense","chapter_title":"Direction Sense","statement":"A person walks 3 km north, 5 km east, then 2 km south. Where is the person relative to the start?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"1 east and 5 north","option_b":"10 km north","option_c":"5 east and 1 north","option_d":"5 west and 1 north","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Net east displacement is 5. Net north displacement is 3 - 2 = 1; therefore the position is 5 east and 1 north.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0599","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"blood-relations","chapter_title":"Blood Relations","statement":"Hina is the mother of Omar. Omar is the brother of Nida. How is Hina related to Nida?","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Aunt","option_b":"Mother","option_c":"Daughter","option_d":"Sister","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Omar and Nida are siblings, and Hina is Omar's mother. Therefore Hina is also Nida's mother.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0600","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"linear-seating","chapter_title":"Linear Seating","statement":"Five students sit in a row. Hadi is left of Iram, Iram is left of Junaid, Junaid is left of Kiran, and Kiran is left of Lara. Who sits in the middle?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Iram","option_b":"Lara","option_c":"Hadi","option_d":"Junaid","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The constraints fix the order as Hadi, Iram, Junaid, Kiran, Lara. The third, or middle, student is Junaid.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0601","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"scheduling","chapter_title":"Scheduling","statement":"A test is scheduled one day after Tuesday. On which day is it scheduled?","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Friday","option_b":"Thursday","option_c":"Tuesday","option_d":"Wednesday","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The day immediately after Tuesday is Wednesday.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0602","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"verbal-analogy","chapter_title":"Verbal Analogy","statement":"Complete the analogy: Knife is to Cut as Pen is to ?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Pen","option_b":"Cut","option_c":"Write","option_d":"Knife","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The relationship in Knife:Cut is the same as in Pen:Write.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0603","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"letter-series","chapter_title":"Letter Series","statement":"Find the next letter: B, E, H, K, ?","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"M","option_b":"B","option_c":"L","option_d":"N","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Letter positions increase by 3 each time, wrapping after Z; the next letter is N.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0604","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"circular-seating","chapter_title":"Circular Seating","statement":"Four people A, B, C, and D sit around a circular table facing the center in that clockwise order, starting with B. Who sits opposite B?","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"D","option_b":"A","option_c":"C","option_d":"B","correct_option":"a","explanation":"With four equally spaced seats, the person two positions away is opposite. That person is D.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0605","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 4, 10, 16, 22, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"28","option_b":"34","option_c":"44","option_d":"27","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Each term increases by 6, so the next is 22 + 6 = 28.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0606","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 3, 6, 12, 24, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"50","option_b":"26","option_c":"48","option_d":"72","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Each term is doubled, so the next is 24 times 2 = 48.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0607","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"coding-and-decoding","chapter_title":"Coding and Decoding","statement":"In a code, LOGIC becomes ORJLF by shifting each letter 3 place(s) forward. How is BRAIN coded?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"BRAIN","option_b":"QLDUE","option_c":"EUDLQ","option_d":"YOXFK","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Shift every letter of BRAIN forward by 3; this gives EUDLQ.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0608","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"direction-sense","chapter_title":"Direction Sense","statement":"A person walks 4 km north, 7 km east, then 3 km south. Where is the person relative to the start?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"7 west and 1 north","option_b":"7 east and 1 north","option_c":"14 km north","option_d":"1 east and 7 north","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Net east displacement is 7. Net north displacement is 4 - 3 = 1; therefore the position is 7 east and 1 north.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0609","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"blood-relations","chapter_title":"Blood Relations","statement":"Sara is the mother of Zain. Zain is the brother of Maya. How is Sara related to Maya?","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Mother","option_b":"Sister","option_c":"Daughter","option_d":"Aunt","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Zain and Maya are siblings, and Sara is Zain's mother. Therefore Sara is also Maya's mother.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0610","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"linear-seating","chapter_title":"Linear Seating","statement":"Five students sit in a row. Ali is left of Bina, Bina is left of Dani, Dani is left of Esha, and Esha is left of Fari. Who sits in the middle?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"to