wo positions away is opposite. That person is B.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0625","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 6, 10, 14, 18, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"21","option_b":"36","option_c":"26","option_d":"22","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Each term increases by 4, so the next is 18 + 4 = 22.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0626","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 5, 10, 20, 40, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"42","option_b":"80","option_c":"82","option_d":"120","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Each term is doubled, so the next is 40 times 2 = 80.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0627","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"coding-and-decoding","chapter_title":"Coding and Decoding","statement":"In a code, FAST becomes KFXY by shifting each letter 5 place(s) forward. How is MATH coded?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"HVOC","option_b":"RFYM","option_c":"MATH","option_d":"MYFR","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Shift every letter of MATH forward by 5; this gives RFYM.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0628","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"direction-sense","chapter_title":"Direction Sense","statement":"A person walks 6 km north, 4 km east, then 5 km south. Where is the person relative to the start?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"4 west and 1 north","option_b":"1 east and 4 north","option_c":"4 east and 1 north","option_d":"15 km north","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Net east displacement is 4. Net north displacement is 6 - 5 = 1; therefore the position is 4 east and 1 north.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0629","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"blood-relations","chapter_title":"Blood Relations","statement":"Hina is the mother of Omar. Omar is the brother of Nida. How is Hina related to Nida?","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Aunt","option_b":"Daughter","option_c":"Mother","option_d":"Sister","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Omar and Nida are siblings, and Hina is Omar's mother. Therefore Hina is also Nida's mother.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0630","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"linear-seating","chapter_title":"Linear Seating","statement":"Five students sit in a row. Ali is left of Bina, Bina is left of Dani, Dani is left of Esha, and Esha is left of Fari. Who sits in the middle?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Bina","option_b":"Dani","option_c":"Ali","option_d":"Fari","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The constraints fix the order as Ali, Bina, Dani, Esha, Fari. The third, or middle, student is Dani.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0631","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"scheduling","chapter_title":"Scheduling","statement":"A test is scheduled one day after Monday. On which day is it scheduled?","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Tuesday","option_b":"Thursday","option_c":"Wednesday","option_d":"Monday","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The day immediately after Monday is Tuesday.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0632","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"verbal-analogy","chapter_title":"Verbal Analogy","statement":"Complete the analogy: Book is to Read as Food is to ?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Eat","option_b":"Read","option_c":"Food","option_d":"Book","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The relationship in Book:Read is the same as in Food:Eat.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0633","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"letter-series","chapter_title":"Letter Series","statement":"Find the next letter: E, G, I, K, ?","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Insufficient information","option_b":"M","option_c":"E","option_d":"L","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Letter positions increase by 2 each time, wrapping after Z; the next letter is M.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0634","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"circular-seating","chapter_title":"Circular Seating","statement":"Four people A, B, C, and D sit around a circular table facing the center in that clockwise order, starting with A. Who sits opposite A?","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"C","option_b":"B","option_c":"D","option_d":"A","correct_option":"a","explanation":"With four equally spaced seats, the person two positions away is opposite. That person is C.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0635","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 7, 13, 19, 25, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"30","option_b":"31","option_c":"37","option_d":"50","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Each term increases by 6, so the next is 25 + 6 = 31.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0636","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 1, 2, 4, 8, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"16","option_b":"18","option_c":"24","option_d":"10","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Each term is doubled, so the next is 8 times 2 = 16.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0637","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"coding-and-decoding","chapter_title":"Coding and Decoding","statement":"In a code, CODE becomes DPEF by shifting each letter 1 place(s) forward. How is TEST coded?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"UTFU","option_b":"SDRS","option_c":"TEST","option_d":"UFTU","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Shift every letter of TEST forward by 1; this gives UFTU.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0638","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"direction-sense","chapter_title":"Direction Sense","statement":"A person walks 7 km north, 6 km east, then 1 km south. Where is the person relative to the start?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Insufficient information","option_b":"14 km north","option_c":"6 east and 6 north","option_d":"6 west and 6 north","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Net east displacement is 6. Net north displacement is 7 - 1 = 6; therefore the position is 6 east and 6 north.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0639","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analyt