","option_c":"Cut","option_d":"Knife","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The relationship in Knife:Cut is the same as in Pen:Write.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0643","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"letter-series","chapter_title":"Letter Series","statement":"Find the next letter: F, I, L, O, ?","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"P","option_b":"R","option_c":"F","option_d":"Q","correct_option":"b","explanation":"Letter positions increase by 3 each time, wrapping after Z; the next letter is R.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0644","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"circular-seating","chapter_title":"Circular Seating","statement":"Four people A, B, C, and D sit around a circular table facing the center in that clockwise order, starting with B. Who sits opposite B?","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"C","option_b":"A","option_c":"D","option_d":"B","correct_option":"c","explanation":"With four equally spaced seats, the person two positions away is opposite. That person is D.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0645","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 8, 10, 12, 14, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"16","option_b":"15","option_c":"18","option_d":"28","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Each term increases by 2, so the next is 14 + 2 = 16.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0646","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 2, 4, 8, 16, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"32","option_b":"48","option_c":"18","option_d":"34","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Each term is doubled, so the next is 16 times 2 = 32.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0647","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"coding-and-decoding","chapter_title":"Coding and Decoding","statement":"In a code, LOGIC becomes NQIKE by shifting each letter 2 place(s) forward. How is BRAIN coded?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"PKCTD","option_b":"BRAIN","option_c":"ZPYGL","option_d":"DTCKP","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Shift every letter of BRAIN forward by 2; this gives DTCKP.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0648","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"direction-sense","chapter_title":"Direction Sense","statement":"A person walks 8 km north, 8 km east, then 2 km south. Where is the person relative to the start?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"8 east and 6 north","option_b":"8 west and 6 north","option_c":"18 km north","option_d":"6 east and 8 north","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Net east displacement is 8. Net north displacement is 8 - 2 = 6; therefore the position is 8 east and 6 north.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0649","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"blood-relations","chapter_title":"Blood Relations","statement":"Amina is the mother of Bilal. Bilal is the brother of Cyrus. How is Amina related to Cyrus?","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Mother","option_b":"Daughter","option_c":"Sister","option_d":"Aunt","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Bilal and Cyrus are siblings, and Am