 Dani, Dani is left of Esha, and Esha is left of Fari. Who sits in the middle?","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Dani","option_b":"Fari","option_c":"Ali","option_d":"Bina","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The constraints fix the order as Ali, Bina, Dani, Esha, Fari. The third, or middle, student is Dani.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0711","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"scheduling","chapter_title":"Scheduling","statement":"A test is scheduled one day after Monday. On which day is it scheduled?","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Monday","option_b":"Thursday","option_c":"Wednesday","option_d":"Tuesday","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The day immediately after Monday is Tuesday.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0712","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"verbal-analogy","chapter_title":"Verbal Analogy","statement":"Complete the analogy: Book is to Read as Food is to ?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Read","option_b":"Food","option_c":"Eat","option_d":"Book","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The relationship in Book:Read is the same as in Food:Eat.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0713","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"letter-series","chapter_title":"Letter Series","statement":"Find the next letter: C, E, G, I, ?","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"K","option_b":"J","option_c":"Insufficient information","option_d":"C","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Letter positions increase by 2 each time, wrapping after Z; the next letter is K.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0714","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"circular-seating","chapter_title":"Circular Seating","statement":"Four people A, B, C, and D sit around a circular table facing the center in that clockwise order, starting with A. Who sits opposite A?","chapter_num":9,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"B","option_b":"A","option_c":"C","option_d":"D","correct_option":"c","explanation":"With four equally spaced seats, the person two positions away is opposite. That person is C.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0715","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 8, 12, 16, 20, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"24","option_b":"40","option_c":"28","option_d":"23","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Each term increases by 4, so the next is 20 + 4 = 24.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0716","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 4, 8, 16, 32, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"64","option_b":"34","option_c":"96","option_d":"66","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Each term is doubled, so the next is 32 times 2 = 64.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0717","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"coding-and-decoding","chapter_title":"Coding and Decoding","statement":"In a code, CODE becomes GSHI by shifting each letter 4 place(s) forward. How is TEST coded?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"XIWX","option_b":"XWIX","option_c":"TEST","option_d":"PAOP","correct_option":"a","explanation":"Shift every letter of TEST