hapter_slug":"number-series","chapter_title":"Number Series","statement":"Find the next number: 2, 4, 8, 16, ?","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"18","option_b":"48","option_c":"32","option_d":"34","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Each term is doubled, so the next is 16 times 2 = 32.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0747","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"coding-and-decoding","chapter_title":"Coding and Decoding","statement":"In a code, FAST becomes HCUV by shifting each letter 2 place(s) forward. How is MATH coded?","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"JVCO","option_b":"MATH","option_c":"OCVJ","option_d":"KYRF","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Shift every letter of MATH forward by 2; this gives OCVJ.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0748","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"direction-sense","chapter_title":"Direction Sense","statement":"A person walks 2 km north, 7 km east, then 2 km south. Where is the person relative to the start?","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"7 west and 0 north","option_b":"11 km north","option_c":"7 east and 0 north","option_d":"0 east and 7 north","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Net east displacement is 7. Net north displacement is 2 - 2 = 0; therefore the position is 7 east and 0 north.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0749","subject":"IQ & Analytical Reasoning","subject_slug":"iq-analytical-reasoning","chapter_slug":"blood-relations","chapter_title":"Blood Relations","statement":"Hina is the mother of Omar. Omar is the brother of Nida. How is Hina related to Nida?","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Aunt","option_b":"Daughter","option_c":"Mother","option_d":"Sister","correct_opti