:"Choose the correct form: She ___ the task yesterday.","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"completed","option_b":"will completing","option_c":"complete","option_d":"is complete","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The time expression 'yesterday' calls for 'completed'.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0754","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"prepositions","chapter_title":"Prepositions","statement":"Choose the correct preposition: They are interested ___ solving the problem.","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"in","option_b":"at","option_c":"with","option_d":"by","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The standard expression requires the preposition 'in'.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0755","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"sentence-correction","chapter_title":"Sentence Correction","statement":"Choose the grammatically correct sentence for set 1.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"He do not know the answer.","option_b":"He does not know the answer.","option_c":"He does not know the answer yesterday yesterday.","option_d":"He does not know a the answer.","correct_option":"b","explanation":"'He does not know the answer.' has correct agreement, tense, and word order.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0756","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"synonyms","chapter_title":"Synonyms","statement":"Choose the closest synonym of 'abundant' in ordinary academic usage.","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"hostile","option_b":"plentiful","option_c":"uncertain","option_d":"scarce","correct_option":"b","explanation":"'plentiful' most nearly matches the meaning of 'abundant'.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0757","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"antonyms","chapter_title":"Antonyms","statement":"Choose the antonym of 'expand' in ordinary academic usage.","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"careful","option_b":"contract","option_c":"steady","option_d":"similar","correct_option":"b","explanation":"'contract' expresses the opposite of 'expand'.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0758","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"contextual-vocabulary","chapter_title":"Contextual Vocabulary","statement":"In the sentence 'Although the route was difficult, the hikers remained resolute.' what does 'resolute' most nearly mean?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"lengthy","option_b":"optional","option_c":"determined","option_d":"careless","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Context shows that 'resolute' means 'determined'.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0759","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"reading-comprehension","chapter_title":"Reading Comprehension","statement":"Read the sentence: Solar panels generate electricity without burning fuel, but their output varies with sunlight. Which statement best captures its main idea?","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"The sentence rejects all technology.","option_b":"Their output depends on sunlight.","option_c":"The author gives no information.","option_d":"Only one detail matters.","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The correct choice restates the central claim without adding or contradicting details.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0760","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"subject-verb-agreement","chapter_title":"Subject Verb Agreement","statement":"Complete the sentence: The committee, along with its chair, ___ meeting today.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"are","option_b":"is","option_c":"were","option_d":"have","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The controlling subject is singular, so 'is' is required.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0761","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"tenses","chapter_title":"Tenses","statement":"Choose the best tense: If I had known, I ___ earlier.","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"arrive","option_b":"had arriving","option_c":"would have arrived","option_d":"will arrived","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The clause structure and time reference require 'would have arrived'.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0762","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"prepositions","chapter_title":"Prepositions","statement":"Choose the correct preposition: The report was divided ___ three sections.","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"by","option_b":"into","option_c":"at","option_d":"to","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The idiomatic construction uses the preposition 'into'.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0763","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"reading-comprehension","chapter_title":"Reading Comprehension","statement":"Read: Because the road was flooded, the match was postponed. Why was the match postponed?","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"The passage does not say.","option_b":"The road was flooded.","option_c":"To increase the cost.","option_d":"Because the output failed.","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The answer follows directly from the stated cause or comparison in the sentence.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0764","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"subject-verb-agreement","chapter_title":"Subject Verb Agreement","statement":"Choose the correct verb: Each of the players ___ on the desk.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"are","option_b":"be","option_c":"were","option_d":"is","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The grammatical head of the subject requires the singular/plural verb 'is'.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0765","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"tenses","chapter_title":"Tenses","statement":"Choose the correct form: She ___ the task every day.","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"walks","option_b":"walked","option_c":"is complete","option_d":"will completing","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The time expression 'every day' calls for 'walks'.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0766","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"prepositions","chapter_title":"Prepositions","statement":"Choose the correct preposition: They are responsible ___ solving the problem.","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"by","option_b":"at","option_c":"with","option_d":"for","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The standard expression requires the preposition 'for'.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0767","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"sentence-correction","chapter_title":"Sentence Correction","statement":"Choose the grammatically correct sentence for set 2.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"She have finished her work.","option_b":"She has finished her work yesterday yesterday.","option_c":"Insufficient information","option_d":"She has finished her work.","correct_option":"d","explanation":"'She has finished her work.' has correct agreement, tense, and word order.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0768","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"synonyms","chapter_title":"Synonyms","statement":"Choose the closest synonym of 'brief' in ordinary academic usage.","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"short","option_b":"scarce","option_c":"hostile","option_d":"uncertain","correct_option":"a","explanation":"'short' most nearly matches the meaning of 'brief'.","difficulty":"hard","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0769","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"antonyms","chapter_title":"Antonyms","statement":"Choose the antonym of 'ancient' in ordinary academic usage.","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"steady","option_b":"modern","option_c":"careful","option_d":"similar","correct_option":"b","explanation":"'modern' expresses the opposite of 'ancient'.","difficulty":"easy","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0770","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"contextual-vocabulary","chapter_title":"Contextual Vocabulary","statement":"In the sentence 'The evidence was ambiguous, so the jury requested clarification.' what does 'ambiguous' most nearly mean?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"careless","option_b":"optional","option_c":"lengthy","option_d":"unclear","correct_option":"d","explanation":"Context shows that 'ambiguous' means 'unclear'.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0771","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"reading-comprehension","chapter_title":"Reading Comprehension","statement":"Read the sentence: Regular revision strengthens memory more effectively than one long session before an exam. Which statement best captures its main idea?","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"Spaced revision supports memory.","option_b":"The author gives no information.","option_c":"Only one detail matters.","option_d":"The sentence rejects all technology.","correct_option":"a","explanation":"The correct choice restates the central claim without adding or contradicting details.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0772","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"subject-verb-agreement","chapter_title":"Subject Verb Agreement","statement":"Complete the sentence: Either the teachers or the principal ___ attending.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"are","option_b":"is","option_c":"were","option_d":"have","correct_option":"b","explanation":"The controlling subject is singular, so 'is' is required.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0773","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"tenses","chapter_title":"Tenses","statement":"Choose the best tense: When the bell rang, they ___ the room.","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"will arrived","option_b":"had arriving","option_c":"left","option_d":"arrive","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The clause structure and time reference require 'left'.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0774","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"prepositions","chapter_title":"Prepositions","statement":"Choose the correct preposition: She insisted ___ checking the figures.","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"by","option_b":"at","option_c":"to","option_d":"on","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The idiomatic construction uses the preposition 'on'.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0775","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"reading-comprehension","chapter_title":"Reading Comprehension","statement":"Read: Mina checked every calculation twice to avoid errors. Why did Mina check each calculation twice?","chapter_num":8,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"The passage does not say.","option_b":"Because the output failed.","option_c":"To avoid errors.","option_d":"To increase the cost.","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The answer follows directly from the stated cause or comparison in the sentence.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0776","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"subject-verb-agreement","chapter_title":"Subject Verb Agreement","statement":"Choose the correct verb: The students in the hall ___ on the desk.","chapter_num":1,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"is","option_b":"be","option_c":"were","option_d":"are","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The grammatical head of the subject requires the singular/plural verb 'are'.","difficulty":"hard","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0777","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"tenses","chapter_title":"Tenses","statement":"Choose the correct form: She ___ the task by next June.","chapter_num":2,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"will completing","option_b":"is complete","option_c":"finished","option_d":"will have finished","correct_option":"d","explanation":"The time expression 'by next June' calls for 'will have finished'.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0778","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"prepositions","chapter_title":"Prepositions","statement":"Choose the correct preposition: They depend ___ solving the problem.","chapter_num":3,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"at","option_b":"with","option_c":"on","option_d":"by","correct_option":"c","explanation":"The standard expression requires the preposition 'on'.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0779","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"sentence-correction","chapter_title":"Sentence Correction","statement":"Choose the grammatically correct sentence for set 3.","chapter_num":4,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"They were waiting outside.","option_b":"They were waiting outside yesterday yesterday.","option_c":"Insufficient information","option_d":"They was waiting outside.","correct_option":"a","explanation":"'They were waiting outside.' has correct agreement, tense, and word order.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0780","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"synonyms","chapter_title":"Synonyms","statement":"Choose the closest synonym of 'candid' in ordinary academic usage.","chapter_num":5,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"uncertain","option_b":"hostile","option_c":"frank","option_d":"scarce","correct_option":"c","explanation":"'frank' most nearly matches the meaning of 'candid'.","difficulty":"medium","source":"past-paper-style","usage_type":"past_paper"},{"external_id":"FAST-0781","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"antonyms","chapter_title":"Antonyms","statement":"Choose the antonym of 'generous' in ordinary academic usage.","chapter_num":6,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"similar","option_b":"steady","option_c":"careful","option_d":"stingy","correct_option":"d","explanation":"'stingy' expresses the opposite of 'generous'.","difficulty":"easy","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0782","subject":"English","subject_slug":"english","chapter_slug":"contextual-vocabulary","chapter_title":"Contextual Vocabulary","statement":"In the sentence 'The new rule is mandatory for every applicant.' what does 'mandatory' most nearly mean?","chapter_num":7,"node_kind":"topic","option_a":"lengthy","option_b":"careless","option_c":"required","option_d":"optional","correct_option":"c","explanation":"Context shows that 'mandatory' means 'required'.","difficulty":"medium","source":"practice","usage_type":"practice"},{"external_id":"FAST-0783","subject":"English"